<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee coops report low temps but no frosts.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee coops report low temps but no frosts.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Key Brazilian coffee regions had another very cold night but cooperatives and weather centres reported early morning temperatures of 2.5 degrees degrees Celsius and above by 0530 local/0830 GMT.</p>
<p>There were no initial reports of frosts at any of the cooperatives or weather stations, with coffee farms normally seeing warmer temperatures than those registered in the towns due to temperature inversion.</p>
<p>Early morning temperatures in degrees Celsius were as follows.</p>
<p>						     June 9	    June 8</p>
<p> PARANA, Londrina region			7			 5</p>
<p> SAO PAULO, Presidente Prudente	     6			 5</p>
<p> SAO PAULO, Franca			     5.5			9</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS, Sao Sebastiao do Paraiso   5			 7</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS, Pocos de Caldas (coop)    2.5			5</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS, Guaxupe			  3			 7</p>
<p>(-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151)</p>
</text>
